index=entra sourcetype="azure:loganalytics:securityevent" (EventID=4728 OR EventID=4732 OR EventID=4756) earliest=-1h latest=now
``` ========================================================================== ```
``` Detection (SPL): Member added to a privileged Active Directory group       ```
``` Lab:             Contoso Health Identity Platform - Splunk second SIEM     ```
``` KQL twin:        lab/kql/ad-privileged-group-change.kql                    ```
``` -------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` STAND-IN: Splunk Enterprise 60-day TRIAL over SecurityEvent REPLAYED from  ```
``` Log Analytics (ingest-from-loganalytics.sh -T SecurityEvent).              ```
```                                                                            ```
``` WHAT IT CATCHES                                                            ```
```   4728 / 4732 / 4756 on DC01 for a pam-policy.json Tier-0 group (matched   ```
```   by well-known SID / RID first, then name: DnsAdmins) = High, or          ```
```   Tier1-Server-Admins = Medium. The actor (Subject) is the Account.        ```
``` MITRE ATT&CK: T1098.007; T1078.002.                                        ```
```                                                                            ```
``` KQL -> SPL TRANSLATION                                                     ```
```   split(TargetSid, "-")[-1]            -> mvindex(split(...), -1)          ```
```   GroupSid in (list) / startswith      -> in() / match(^S-1-5-21-)         ```
```                                                                            ```
``` SCHEDULE: PT5M / PT1H, severity from the Severity column, throttled 1 h    ```
``` per Account + Severity.                                                    ```
``` ========================================================================== ```
``` @stanza Contoso - Member added to a privileged AD group ```
``` @conf description = Member added to a Tier-0 (or Tier1-Server-Admins) AD group on DC01, matched by well-known SID/RID. KQL twin: lab/kql/ad-privileged-group-change.kql ```
``` @conf disabled = 0 ```
``` @conf enableSched = 1 ```
``` @conf cron_schedule = */5 * * * * ```
``` @conf dispatch.earliest_time = -1h ```
``` @conf dispatch.latest_time = now ```
``` @conf counttype = number of events ```
``` @conf relation = greater than ```
``` @conf quantity = 0 ```
``` @conf alert.track = 1 ```
``` @conf alert.severity = 5 ```
``` @conf alert.expires = 7d ```
``` @conf alert.digest_mode = 0 ```
``` @conf alert.suppress = 1 ```
``` @conf alert.suppress.fields = Account,Severity ```
``` @conf alert.suppress.period = 1h ```
``` @conf request.ui_dispatch_app = search ```
``` @conf request.ui_dispatch_view = search ```
| where in(EventID, 4728, 4732, 4756)
| eval Host=upper(mvindex(split(coalesce(Computer, ""), "."), 0))
| where in(Host, "DC01")
| eval GroupName=TargetUserName, GroupSid=TargetSid
| eval GroupRid=mvindex(split(coalesce(GroupSid, ""), "-"), -1)
| eval GroupTier=case(in(GroupSid, "S-1-5-32-544", "S-1-5-32-548", "S-1-5-32-549", "S-1-5-32-550", "S-1-5-32-551"), "tier0", match(coalesce(GroupSid, ""), "^S-1-5-21-") AND in(GroupRid, "512", "518", "519", "520", "526", "527"), "tier0", lower(coalesce(GroupName, ""))=="dnsadmins", "tier0", lower(coalesce(GroupName, ""))=="tier1-server-admins", "tier1", true(), null())
| where isnotnull(GroupTier)
| eval Account=lower(SubjectUserName), AccountDomain=SubjectDomainName, AccountSid=SubjectUserSid
| eval NewMember=if(isnotnull(MemberName) AND MemberName!="" AND MemberName!="-", MemberName, MemberSid)
| eval Severity=if(GroupTier=="tier0", "High", "Medium")
| sort 0 - _time
| table TimeGenerated, Severity, GroupName, GroupSid, GroupTier, NewMember, MemberSid, Account, AccountDomain, AccountSid, Host, Computer, EventID
